Task 1 - Write a Java program called FoodieBalanceChecker that takes an integer input for wallet balance and prints 'Low Balance Warning.'
         if the balance is less than 100, otherwise prints 'Sufficient Balance.' using an if-else statement.
Answer - 
        import java.util.Scanner;
        public class hello
        {
            public static void main(String[] args)
            {
                Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
                System.out.println("Welcome to Foodie balance Checker");
                System.out.println("Enter your Wallet balance");
                int bal=sc.nextInt();
                if(bal>=100)
                {
                    System.out.println("Sufficent Balance");
                }
                else
                {
                    System.out.println("Low Balance");
                }
            }
        }
